{"name":"Seagrass","hex":"#bcc6a2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seagrass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grass-like marine plants that grow underwater in salt water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagrass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seagrass","blocks":[{"text":"Seagrasses are the only embryophytes which grow in marine environments. There are about 60 species of fully marine seagrasses which belong to four families, all in the order Alismatales. Seagrasses evolved from terrestrial plants which recolonised the ocean 70 to 100 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Zostera_marina_-_National_Museum_of_Nature_and_Science%2C_Tokyo_-_DSC07663.JPG/330px-Zostera_marina_-_National_Museum_of_Nature_and_Science%2C_Tokyo_-_DSC07663.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seagrass","wikidata":"Q646660"},{"title":"Seagrass (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Seagrass is a 2023 Canadian drama film, written and directed by Meredith Hama-Brown. Hama-Brown's full-length feature debut, the film stars Ally Maki as Judith, a woman who is at a family retreat with her husband Steve and their children following the death of her mother, where she and Steve are coping with tensions in their marriage arising from their status as an interracial couple."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/Seagrass_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seagrass_(film)","wikidata":"Q121200650"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Seagrass_evolution.png/500px-Seagrass_evolution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Seagrass_evolution.png/500px-Seagrass_evolution.png?utm_source=en.w